# ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Cluster protocol / experiment directories
#
# These hold SOURCE, not outputs: 26 .sbatch, 6 .py, 9 protocol .md, plus
# ~1.1 MB of small .json/.csv result artifacts that are the evidence trail
# for the thesis. They are tracked deliberately.
#
# Only genuinely generated output is excluded below. These rules are
# prospective -- no such files exist yet -- so that a future Slurm run cannot
# drag logs or checkpoints into git.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------
experiments/**/logs/
experiments/**/checkpoints/
cluster_protocol_*/**/logs/
cluster_protocol_*/**/checkpoints/
*.out
*.err
slurm-*.out

# ---------------------------------------------------------------
# NO-OP LINES -- kept for the record, deliberately left for you to decide.
#
# Git ignores .gitignore for paths that are already tracked, so each of these
# does nothing today. To make any of them real you must first untrack it:
#     git rm --cached -r <path>
#
#   evaluation/            5 files tracked
#   semantic_constraints/  15 files tracked
#   allenamenti.md         tracked
#   .idea/                 6 files tracked (also listed above)
#
# Left as-is because untracking 27 files is your call, not mine.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------
evaluation/
semantic_constraints/
allenamenti.md
*.md
*.png
*.csv
*.sbatch
experiments/

